WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.100
Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.467
is a talented actor
and comedian you know

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.400
from shows like "Community"
and "The Masked Singer"

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.000
and films such as
"The Hangover,"

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.200
"Knocked Up,"
and "Crazy Rich Asians."

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.834
He stars in "The Pentaverate,"

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.300
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.367
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.501
-This is awesome, man!

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.801
I've always wanted
to be kidnapped.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:21.067
It's been one of my dreams.
So...bucket list!

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.367
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:25.434
-You guys mind telling me
where we're going?

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.400
No? Okay, cool.
Spoils the mystery.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.234
Yep. Respect.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.033
-Apply the blindfold, please.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:34.334
-Blindfold.
Okay, yes, please. [ Laughs ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.901
My safe word is "excelsior."

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.100
♪ Ahh ♪

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.133
Oh, it's the pilot.
Why is it on the pilot?

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.200
Is this, like,
a "Fifty Shades" type deal?

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.868
-Please welcome back
to the show our good friend

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.167
Ken Jeong, everybody!

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:57.434
♪♪

00:00:57.434 --> 00:01:03.934
♪♪

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:06.367
Welcome back, my friend.
How are you?

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:10.367
-Thank you.
It is so good to be here live.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.434
-It's so lovely
to have you here live.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.501
-God, the last few times,
it's been over Zoom.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.734
-We've Zoomed it a few times.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:16.901
It's great to have you here
in person.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.234
It's also --
They were very lucky

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.667
to have you in person
in Sacramento.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:23.667
You were honored for Asian-
American Pacific Islander Month.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:27.467
-Yeah, there is --
In California, they --

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.067
it's Asian Pacific
Islander Heritage Month,

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.667
and they honored seven honorees
in excellence

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:36.400
in different fields,
where there was activism.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.901
Mine was overacting.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:41.167
And so it was really great!

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.367
And it was such an honor.

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:48.501
And I, honestly, in all
seriousness, want to thank you,

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:52.868
because I think the last time
I was on the show via Zoom,

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.434
you let me talk about,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.601
you know, just in terms
of what had happened in Atlanta

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:59.434
a year ago and all the various
efforts to stop Asian hate.

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:03.033
So thank you for giving me
the platform and thank you

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.601
for continuing to raise
awareness on all issues.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.767
-Well, thank you.
-Thank you. I appreciate that.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.868
No, no, it's -- Yeah.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.901
-I will say,
I'm a little jealous.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:18.434
You got to do this show
with Mike Myers.

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:21.567
"The Pentaverate" is a
Mike Myers show, six episodes,

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.534
where Mike plays
eight characters.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:26.601
And only Mike Myers
could play more characters

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:27.868
than actual episodes.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:30.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:34.100
In my career, I can barely
play one, you know?

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:37.634
And so, honestly, it was one
of my favorite projects

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.834
I've ever been involved in,
in my life,

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.300
because Mike
is one of my heroes.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.100
He's one of the reasons
I got into comedy.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.000
He's one of the reasons
I left my day job,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.067
you know, as a doctor.

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.801
He's that powerful
in my worldview.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.334
-Yeah.
-You know, I will leave

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.200
the most stable field
of medicine

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.534
only through the power
of a Mike Myers

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.400
that will allow me to overact

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.868
and get an excellent award
in Sacramento.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.167
That's what I'm saying.
You know?

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.834
-I like you telling --

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.601
-Westside! Yeah.

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.234
-I like you -- the idea of you

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:11.901
telling the head
of a medical institution

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.767
that you were leaving and
then, like, showing a picture

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.300
of Fat Bastard and being like,
"It was him.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.567
-It was him!

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.501
-This man made
a very convincing case."

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:22.501
-"I'm gonna get inside
his belly!" Yeah.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.434
-And he wrote this part
with you in mind,

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.767
which is, I mean --
What high praise.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:30.334
-I mean, the whole thing has
been so surreal to be a part of

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:34.467
and now so sublime
to even talk about it.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.901
I've known Mike for a few years,
since the days of him

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:38.467
hosting "The Gong Show."
-Yeah.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.634
-He was playing a character,
also -- Tommy Maitland.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:43.400
So we got to be good buddies
just hanging out afterwards.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.267
Afterwards,
they would always have --

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:46.534
Like, when we'd wrap,

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:49.033
they turned the whole
stage system at Sony

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.234
into a -- into a bar.
-That's fantastic.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.100
-And I literally went on
"The Gong Show"

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.400
I think six times just so
I could drink with Mike Myers.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.601
That was my only goal.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.400
And so we would hang out
and talk.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.601
And then, a couple years later,

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.834
he told me he wrote
a part with me in mind.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:07.334
And, of course, I was just like,
"I'll be your medic.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.100
I'll do whatever you want.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.234
And just to watch his process,
truly he's the GOAT

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:14.667
in terms of, like,
he's not just the star.

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.801
He's the showrunner.
He is the guy.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:19.634
Literally on the call sheet, it
says "Showrunner, Mike Myers."

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.834
So when he's writing
and creating his own universe

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.467
of all these characters
with his specificity and tone.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.167
And then he's so involved,
like, in the post

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.767
and the marketing of it.
Just I've never seen

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:35.200
a more complete performer
in comedy than Mike.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.234
And it truly is, again,
just an honor to be a part of.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.601
-Yeah, the few times
I've been lucky enough

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.400
to be in a room with him,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.767
you realize there's this
incredible attention to detail

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.467
and how hard he works

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.400
to make it look as easy
as he makes it look.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.434
-It was almost like improv
comedy summer camp for me.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:53.801
It really didn't matter to me

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.601
what my involvement was
at the end.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.701
I just wanted -- He was, like,
coaching me

00:04:57.701 --> 00:05:00.100
and guiding me through it,
and he gave me a wig.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.767
-He gave you a super-fun wig.
-He gave me a super --

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:04.934
-The kind of wig
you probably should have.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:07.200
-Probably, yes, you know?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.367
I think I could be an influencer
with that wig.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.100
-Yeah, I think so, too.
-I think I could. TikTok!

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.968
-I'd listen to what
this guy had to say

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.767
about vacation spots
and skin care.

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.200
-Yes! Yes! Yeah, exactly.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.167
"Take care of the pores, yo."

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.567
-You know,
with you and Mike involved,

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.167
I thought there might be
a chance for some nudity.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.133
And there is.
-And there is.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.000
-But kind of
a little heartbroken.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.701
-Why?
-It wasn't you.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.267
-What?!

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:38.267
The shocking part of the nudity
is that I'm not nude in it.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:39.834
-Yeah.
-It's out front.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.434
It's progressive.
-Yeah.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.234
-Been there, done that,
for a lot of money.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:47.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:51.634
And so it really
was just, again --

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.834
Watching -- Watching
Mike go is something else.

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:58.033
-And the "SNL" makeup genius,
Louie --

00:05:58.033 --> 00:05:59.901
-Yes, shout-out
to Louie Zakarian.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:02.033
-Yes, yes.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.667
-He does all the prosthetics
and makeup on "SNL."

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:10.000
He flew in, I think, right
after the finale to London.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.334
And to see hair and makeup,
to see British hair and --

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:17.534
"Oh, no, King Louie is coming!
Oh, we've got to be careful!"

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:19.467
They had the red carpet
out for him.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:21.801
And he is the nicest,
most humble guy.

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:24.400
And honestly, this,
"Pentaverate," to me,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.501
is just as much Louie's show
as it is Mike's,

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:29.434
'cause you really get to see
all the work and all the hours

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:31.300
that it takes to play
the different characters.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.901
I can't say enough great things
about both Louie and Mike.

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.534
It was just --
I'm just so honored.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:41.234
-I was very excited to hear
Apple TV's "The Afterparty"

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.868
is coming back
for a second season.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.100
Even more excited to hear
that you're joining the cast

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.467
for season two. That's great.
-Yes, thank you.

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:49.000
Just hot off the presses.
It got announced.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.467
I'll be in season two
of "The Afterparty"

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:54.767
by the geniuses
Chris Miller and Phil Lord.

00:06:54.767 --> 00:06:57.334
They did "Lego Movie," "Cloudy
with a Chance of Meatballs.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:58.968
-Great guys, as well.
-Great guys.

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:02.033
And it's actually --
Me and my wife,

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:04.267
it's our favorite show
to binge-watch.

00:07:04.267 --> 00:07:06.701
And I literally
was just watching it,

00:07:06.701 --> 00:07:08.434
and Ben Schwartz
is a buddy of mine.

00:07:08.434 --> 00:07:11.367
I'm watching, and he just
steals the season for me.

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:13.667
And I'm like, "Oh, my gosh.
It's my favorite show.

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:15.534
I wish I was relevant
and young enough

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.467
to be on, you know,
that kind of show."

00:07:17.467 --> 00:07:19.200
And just to get the call

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.133
to be a part of it, again,
is just so surreal.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:22.834
-I'm gonna ask a true question.

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:26.234
Will your wife be less inclined
to watch it if you're in it?

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:28.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:36.634
-I'll never tell!

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.434
-Ken Jeong, everybody!

00:07:38.434 --> 00:07:40.801
"The Pentaverate"
is streaming now on Netflix.

